{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>You shall not show favoritism in judgment</b> Tagin on the peh, to say: open your mouth for the mute." "<b>As the small, the great, you shall hear</b> Meaning: as small they should be in your eyes — while they stand before you, both should be in your eyes like wicked men; and when they depart from before you, both should be in your eyes like great ones — meaning, like righteous men." "<b>תשמעון</b> Two times in the Masorah: this one, and the other: \"a prophet I will raise up for you… to him you shall listen (תשמעון)\" — even though I command you \"as the small, as the great, you shall hear,\" if a case comes before you involving a prophet and a Torah scholar, \"to him you shall listen\" first." "<b>For the judgment</b> Tagin on the alef — as though Gehenna is open beneath it." "<b>For the judgment is Elohim's</b> And adjacent to it: \"and the matter that is too hard for you\" — to say: whoever stiffens his neck against the judge, it is as though he stiffens against the Shekhinah." "<b>And the matter</b> Three times in the Masorah: here, and: \"and this matter I cannot do,\" and: \"and the matter that we spoke, I and you.\" Because he said \"and the matter that is too hard for you,\" it came to this — that he did not know what the daughters of Zelophehad knew. And this is: \"and this matter I cannot do\" — that he could not do it. And who did it? \"And the matter that we spoke, I and you\" — and adjacent to it: \"HaShem be between me and you,\" etc., as written: \"and Moses brought their judgment before HaShem.\""], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:08:34.899406003Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}